From: PS4 port
Subject: [PATCH] orbis: a 4 KiB guard page on a 16 KiB-page console

With s_fast_map promoted (patch 0004) the fault moved rather than went away:

    fatal: signal 11 - SIGSEGV (bad address), si_code 2, fault address 0x800f62000

That is s_code_storage + 4096, exactly. JitCodeBuffer::Initialize mprotects the first guard_size
bytes to PROT_NONE and then gives the recompiler `buffer + guard_size` to write into. mprotect on
this console works in 16 KiB granules - the platform's real page size, measured twice by
orbis-compat - so a 4096-byte guard is rounded UP to 16384 and the recompiler's first write lands
12 KiB inside the guard.

⚠ THE SAME 4096 ASSUMPTION IS ALL OVER THIS TREE AND MOST OF IT IS HARMLESS. It only bites where a
length is used as an OFFSET afterwards, as it is here. Xbyak's ALIGN_PAGE_SIZE is also 4096 and
causes no trouble, because it only ever rounds allocation sizes up.

diff --git a/src/core/cpu_code_cache.cpp b/src/core/cpu_code_cache.cpp
--- a/src/core/cpu_code_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/core/cpu_code_cache.cpp
@@ -44,7 +44,21 @@
 #define CODE_WRITE_FAULT_THRESHOLD_FOR_SLOWMEM 10
 
 #ifdef USE_STATIC_CODE_BUFFER
+#ifdef __ORBIS__
+// ⚠ 4096 IS NOT A PAGE ON THIS CONSOLE AND THE GUARD TURNS INTO A TRAP AT THAT SIZE.
+// JitCodeBuffer::Initialize mprotects the first guard_size bytes to PROT_NONE, then hands the
+// recompiler `buffer + guard_size` to write into. mprotect here works in 16 KiB granules - the
+// platform's real page size - so a 4096-byte request is rounded UP to 16384, and the address the
+// recompiler is told to start at lands 12 KiB inside the guard it was meant to sit after.
+// Measured, after s_fast_map was promoted and the fault moved:
+//
+//     fatal: signal 11 - SIGSEGV, si_code 2, fault address 0x800f62000
+//
+// which is s_code_storage + 4096 exactly. One granule makes the guard a guard again.
+static constexpr uint32_t RECOMPILER_GUARD_SIZE = 16384;
+#else
 static constexpr uint32_t RECOMPILER_GUARD_SIZE = 4096;
+#endif
 alignas(Recompiler::CODE_STORAGE_ALIGNMENT) static uint8_t
   s_code_storage[RECOMPILER_CODE_CACHE_SIZE + RECOMPILER_FAR_CODE_CACHE_SIZE];
 #endif
